infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Pick a transporter on delivery, not syntax
  desc Same handler API; what differs is whether a message survives — and the price of durability
  compares
    - label At-most-once (lossy)
      children
        - label TCP
          desc Point-to-point, no broker to run
        - label Redis pub/sub
          desc Cheap fan-out; only live subscribers receive it
        - label NATS core
          desc Low-latency subjects; JetStream adds persistence
        - label Lost on no listener
          desc Nothing persisted, nothing to replay
    - label At-least-once (durable)
      children
        - label RabbitMQ
          desc Durable queues, acks, requeue on failure
        - label Kafka
          desc Partitioned log, offset replay, order per partition
        - label Redelivery happens
          desc Broker re-sends on ack failure or rebalance
        - label Consumers must be idempotent
          desc Or you double-charge the card
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
